<title>SPAIN: Spain's CNMV lifts suspension on utility shares.</title>
<headline>Spain's CNMV lifts suspension on utility shares.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish stock market watchdog CNMV has lifted the suspension on trading in Hidrocantabrico, Electra de Viesgo and Saltos de Nansa, a spokesman for the Spanish bourse said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The decision follows statements by Hidrocantabrico and Endesa denying press reports that Cantabrico intends to buy the state-owned company's stakes in Viesgo and Nansa.</p>
<p>The shares were suspended from trading on Monday.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
